WEBVTT

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:13.650
<b>Holy Empire of Lubelius  "Inner Sanctum"</b>

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:21.650
Ow, ow, ow...

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:23.820
The heck's your problem?!

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.170
This place is supposed to be sacred.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.920
So why's there a vampire here?!

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:33.880
Hold your tongue, vermin! 
You taint the holy throne of God!

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:38.060
Any who disgrace the one and only 
god, Luminus, will not be tolerated!

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:39.970
Yikes!

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.710
Begone!

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.550
This ain't good...

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:07.580
<b>That Time I Got 
Reincarnated as a Slime</b>

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:22.450
Episode 38: A Meeting of Humans and Monsters

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:22.490
Well, Laplace, it sounds like 
you've been through a lot.

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:26.610
So did you find out what the 
Western Holy Church really is?

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:29.290
Well, actually...

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:32.290
Security was so tight, 
I couldn't get anywhere!

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:36.280
Hmm... And? Surely you 
found a hint, at least?

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:40.800
Man, since I went through hell to get 
this info, I was gonna sell it high...

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:43.580
But I know you're a liar.

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:45.600
Yer so mean.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:51.440
I really feel bad for the slime who's got 
no idea he's wrapped up in your scheme.

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.190
After all...

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:58.190
You <i>are</i> the weirdo with the twisted ambition 
hidin' behind the face of the Grandmaster,

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:01.130
Yuuki Kagurazaka.

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:03.440
I'm honored by your praise,

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:05.580
but you can't back out of the job.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:07.830
Man, you're indomitable.

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:09.620
Now, don't say that.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:12.200
I've already prepared the 
reward I promised you.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.450
What?! Then...

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:16.990
Yes. The soul of your alliance's 
president, which was inside me,

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:19.220
was safely transferred to a homunculus.

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:22.470
The president... is finally comin' back!

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:24.460
Where is he?! Lemme see 'im!

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:27.320
Relax. He's been right there this whole time.

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:28.020
What?!

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:33.400
Huh? This... lovely lady?

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:40.550
What the heck's with that look? 
Did yer tastes change?

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:43.210
Quiet, Laplace.

00:03:43.210 --> 00:03:46.080
You dare take that attitude with me, 
the Demon Lord Kazalim,

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:48.540
<b>Kagali
(Formerly Demon Lord Kazalim)</b>

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.540
when you haven't seen me in 200 years?

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:52.520
Welcome back, President Kazalim.

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:55.440
The Moderate Harlequin Alliance 
has been waitin' for ya.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:58.260
Myself, Footman, Tear...

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:00.000
and Clayman, too.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:05.140
Sorry to put a damper on 
your touching reunion,

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:08.810
but the Demon Lord Kazalim 
isn't fully revived yet.

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:10.250
True.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:14.300
In all honesty, my power is nowhere 
near the power I had in my prime.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:17.690
Leon Cromwell... Curse that bastard!

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:21.250
I wish you wouldn't complain 
about your new body.

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:23.220
It was pretty expensive, you know.

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:24.970
I know that, boss.

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:27.160
It was custom-made in Thalion, right?

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:30.900
It's weak, and it's not my preferred look,

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:34.930
but it's far better than not having 
a material body I can move on my own.

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:37.420
Hey!

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:39.800
Are you ever going to 
stop laughing, Laplace?!

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:44.170
Anyway, do you mind if 
we get to the point now?

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:48.050
You got something on the 
Western Holy Church, right?

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:53.560
Okay. If the president calls you 
"boss," you're my boss, too.

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:56.750
I'll tell ya what I know 
without askin' for any deals.

00:04:58.390 --> 00:05:02.530
There was nothin' in the 
Western Holy Church that seemed dodgy.

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:04.680
I mean, believers go there to worship.

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:07.910
They ain't gonna put anything 
scary in plain sight.

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:11.900
So I decided to head to the 
top of the sacred mountain.

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:14.100
Thought I might find somethin' 
in the inner sanctum

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:16.370
that only their cloistered emperor can enter.

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:22.110
And then... this important-lookin' 
vampire dude shot a red beam at me

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:24.970
and roughed me up good.

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:27.510
Wait, how are you still alive?

00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:30.200
You said he shot a red beam at you?

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:31.260
Yep.

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:33.880
That's called Blood Ray. It turns 
blood into magic particles,

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:35.860
which are fired as a beam.

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:41.020
It's the signature attack of the Demon Lord 
Valentine, also known as the Blood Tyrant.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.580
A Demon Lord?! You serious?!

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:45.710
Fleeing was the right choice, Laplace.

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:48.900
That man was an even 
match for me in my prime.

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:50.780
Damn!

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:53.550
Every time I fought him in the past,

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:55.820
the damage to the surroundings was immense.

00:05:55.820 --> 00:06:00.540
So we had a discussion, which led 
to the custom of the majority vote.

00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:03.070
Are you talking about Walpurgis?

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:06.080
Yes. The requirement of three votes 
to move forward on a proposal

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:08.980
is a remnant of the time when 
there were seven Demon Lords.

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:12.570
So if we know that guy was 
the Demon Lord Valentine,

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:15.060
I wonder what he was doing there.

00:06:15.490 --> 00:06:17.380
The most likely explanation

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:20.580
is that the cloistered emperor 
was actually a Demon Lord.

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:24.540
Valentine sees humans and 
demihumans as no more than food.

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:28.740
If such a man is claiming to 
be the guardian of humanity...

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:32.040
There must be something to it.

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:35.360
Regardless, this is useful information.

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:37.600
Well done, Laplace.

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:41.060
I'd like to investigate the 
Western Holy Church further,

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:45.210
but if the Demon Lord Valentine is 
there, I guess we can't be careless.

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:50.280
Well, if ya just wanna lure out a 
Demon Lord, that should be doable, right?

00:06:51.730 --> 00:06:55.170
Clayman, Demon Lord Milim, 
and Demon Lord Frey.

00:06:55.170 --> 00:06:58.230
There's a lot an alliance of 
three Demon Lords can do, right?

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:02.630
So let 'em have Walpurgis.

00:07:06.390 --> 00:07:08.440
That's quite clever, for you.

00:07:08.440 --> 00:07:09.900
Ain't it?

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:15.700
Now, what's that squishy one gonna do?

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:23.890
Next is our new second secretary, Diablo.

00:07:23.890 --> 00:07:26.170
A pleasure to make your acquaintance.

00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:28.920
And the caretaker of the Forest of Jura...

00:07:29.690 --> 00:07:31.680
I am the Dryad Treyni.

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:36.250
This concludes the introductions 
of our members from Tempest.

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:39.180
I will now introduce our guests.

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:43.540
From the Armed Nation of 
Dwargon, King Gazel Dwargo.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:48.090
From the Sorcerous Dynasty 
of Thalion, Archduke Erald.

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:49.440
It's a pleasure.

00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:52.500
From the Animal Kingdom of 
Eurazania's Warrior Brigade,

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:56.570
the Three Beastketeers, Lady Albis, 
Lady Suphia, and Sir Phobio.

00:07:57.180 --> 00:08:00.970
From the Kingdom of 
Blumund, Guildmaster Fuze.

00:08:00.970 --> 00:08:02.210
Uh... Yes.

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:05.700
And representing the future 
Kingdom of Falmuth,

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:08.970
Sir Grucius, Lady Mjurran, and Sir Youm.

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:12.760
Nice to meet you.

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:18.690
<i>Wow, pretty prominent bunch 
of people we've got here...</i>

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:22.560
Shuna, what's Veldora doing?

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:27.070
Yes, he has changed clothes 
and should arrive shortly.

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:34.280
Sorry to keep you all waiting!

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:36.790
Oh, that looks wonderful on you!

00:08:36.790 --> 00:08:38.770
And it appears to be the perfect size!

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:42.120
Right? It is truly a nice outfit!

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:43.780
You have my compliments!

00:08:43.780 --> 00:08:45.280
Thank you!

00:08:46.390 --> 00:08:48.940
Rimuru, is this another of your subordinates?

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:51.880
I haven't seen him before.

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:55.510
Yeah. Let me introduce you 
all to my sworn friend.

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:56.840
This is Veldora-kun.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:08:59.060
<i>Veldora?</i>

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:00.170
<i>Veldora?</i>

00:09:00.170 --> 00:09:01.890
<i>Vel...dora?</i>

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:11.900
I am the Storm Dragon, Veldora Tempest!

00:09:12.590 --> 00:09:16.340
Very few people have had 
a chance to speak with me.

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:18.390
You are all extremely fortunate!

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:20.400
Consider this a great honor!

00:09:22.010 --> 00:09:24.000
Uh-oh. He passed out.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:25.210
I don't blame him.

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:27.470
Huh, was he overcome with emotion?

00:09:27.470 --> 00:09:28.710
That's not it!

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:33.180
Hey, Veldora, we're about to 
have a serious discussion here.

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:34.800
Don't get in the way, okay?

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:37.060
During the meeting, I'd like 
you to act as an advisor,

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:39.430
and please, behave yourself.

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:42.800
You can even go take a walk if you want.

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:46.730
That's cold, BFF! Bestie!

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:49.440
Don't try to leave me out like that!

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:50.670
Rimuru!

00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:53.180
I need to talk to you.

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:55.700
Uh... So do I.

00:09:56.550 --> 00:10:01.450
<i>And so our very important meeting to 
determine the future of Tempest...</i>

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:04.630
<i>was called off before it even began.</i>

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:10.000
If you'll excuse me, then.

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:19.510
What's the meaning of this?! 
The Storm Dragon Veldora has returned?!

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:22.260
Um, to put it really simply...

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:24.650
Before you do that, let me say one thing.

00:10:24.650 --> 00:10:25.810
S-Sure...

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:31.810
The emperor of the Sorcerous Dynasty of 
Thalion has entrusted me with full authority.

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:36.190
What I say dictates Thalion's position.

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:38.360
Now, with that in mind...

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:40.330
Let's hear your explanation.

00:10:40.330 --> 00:10:41.740
Okay, okay.

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:44.950
I promise I'll tell the truth.

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:49.500
<i>I told them the whole story.</i>

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:52.790
<i>That I reincarnated into 
this world as a slime,</i>

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:56.460
<i>that I met Veldora in the Sealed Cave,</i>

00:10:57.350 --> 00:11:00.220
<i>and that I became a Demon 
Lord for certain reasons,</i>

00:11:00.650 --> 00:11:03.030
<i>revived my friends who had been killed,</i>

00:11:03.030 --> 00:11:06.260
<i>and released Veldora's seal.</i>

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:11.190
And that brings us to today.

00:11:12.130 --> 00:11:13.190
Uh, hey...

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:15.530
I never imagined this.

00:11:15.530 --> 00:11:18.630
It was problematic enough 
that you became a Demon Lord,

00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:21.220
but you had an even bigger 
problem waiting for us...

00:11:21.220 --> 00:11:23.200
Please! No need for such praise!

00:11:24.810 --> 00:11:29.670
Mister Rimuru, is he really 
the Storm Dragon Veldora?

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:30.790
Is he? I wonder!

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:32.520
No, I know he is.

00:11:33.350 --> 00:11:35.900
No human or monster is foolish enough to use

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:38.510
the name of the Evil Dragon in jest.

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:40.510
<i>Good point.</i>

00:11:41.270 --> 00:11:42.490
Still...

00:11:42.490 --> 00:11:44.010
What to do?

00:11:44.650 --> 00:11:47.150
Do we make this news public or conceal it?

00:11:47.150 --> 00:11:50.020
Either way, the Western Nations 
shouldn't pose a problem.

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:55.290
As for the Sorcerous Dynasty of Thalion, 
I need only report to the emperor.

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:56.810
The only problem is...

00:11:56.810 --> 00:11:59.120
The Western Holy Church.

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:01.910
We cannot keep this a secret from them.

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:06.280
Of all the Dragons, they regard the 
Storm Dragon with particular hostility.

00:12:06.690 --> 00:12:10.790
They've probably already discovered 
that the Evil Dragon is back.

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:16.120
<i>These two seem to get along pretty well.</i>

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:17.210
Are you listening, Rimuru?!

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:18.420
Y-Yes!

00:12:18.540 --> 00:12:21.440
We need you to give serious 
thought to this matter!

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:23.130
Sorry.

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:27.140
Well, I was planning to spread 
the word about Veldora, anyway.

00:12:27.530 --> 00:12:30.640
And it doesn't seem like there'll be 
any avoiding the Western Holy Church...

00:12:30.990 --> 00:12:32.670
So we'll have to do <i>something</i>.

00:12:34.540 --> 00:12:37.160
If that is the decision, 
I have no complaints.

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:40.110
A Demon Lord joining forces 
with the Evil Dragon...

00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:43.480
Could there be a more 
troubling turn of events?

00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:45.160
It's not a funny joke at all.

00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:48.290
That said, this is fortunate.

00:12:48.930 --> 00:12:49.910
It is?

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:56.290
Since I was able to take part 
in this private meeting,

00:12:56.290 --> 00:13:01.880
I gained the best possible knowledge with 
which to determine my nation's position.

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:04.940
Ah...

00:13:04.940 --> 00:13:08.120
It would be foolish to pick a fight with 
a nation that's home to both a Demon Lord

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:09.400
and the Evil Dragon.

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:11.080
Precisely.

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:12.430
I see.

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:18.090
So you're saying that even if the 
Western Holy Church becomes our enemy,

00:13:18.090 --> 00:13:19.930
you'll take our side. 
Is that a fair conclusion?

00:13:19.930 --> 00:13:25.960
Rimuru, you should really learn 
the art of the unspoken message.

00:13:25.960 --> 00:13:27.240
R-Right...

00:13:28.140 --> 00:13:32.110
I'm saying that I won't 
expose my country to danger

00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:34.650
when there's no real reason to be hostile.

00:13:34.650 --> 00:13:37.750
We are under no obligation 
to the Western Holy Church.

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:39.180
Understand?

00:13:39.180 --> 00:13:40.080
Yeah.

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:43.050
It'll be reassuring to have you on our side.

00:13:43.470 --> 00:13:45.260
But... Erald-san...

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:48.360
We haven't established diplomatic 
relations with Thalion.

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:50.410
Why are you being so cordial?

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:57.310
Mister Rimuru, in formal settings, please
address me with both my name and my title.

00:13:57.310 --> 00:13:59.650
You are the leader of a nation.

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:02.900
There's no need to humble yourself 
before another nation's authority.

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:07.690
Though I don't mind you addressing 
me as you just did, or with "Mister."

00:14:08.920 --> 00:14:10.820
Okay. Thanks.

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:15.000
That aside, allow me to answer your question.

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:17.860
Since it was my daughter, Ere—

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:24.540
I mean, Eryune, who told you 
how to become a Demon Lord,

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:27.510
I am charged with taking 
responsibility for that.

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:31.150
Now, tell me this fairy tale 
about reviving the dead.

00:14:31.150 --> 00:14:32.050
Sure.

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:38.690
After all, one could say that my 
daughter created a Demon Lord.

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:43.020
But only the emperor and I know this.

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:46.430
This is why I came here personally

00:14:46.430 --> 00:14:50.410
to judge you for myself, with the 
possibility of dispatching an army in kind

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:53.030
in case I deemed it necessary.

00:14:53.750 --> 00:14:56.040
And what judgment have you made?

00:14:56.570 --> 00:14:59.790
As I said earlier, I choose friendship.

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:02.080
That's the obvious choice, of course.

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:08.020
My country had every intention of backing 
Tempest as a friendly nation from the start.

00:15:09.390 --> 00:15:12.220
Of course, this arrangement 
is not without its problems.

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:15.340
The army of Falmuth that 
Mister Rimuru annihilated

00:15:15.340 --> 00:15:17.310
produced far too many casualties.

00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:20.820
A Demon Lord who has killed 20,000 men...

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:22.520
Don't worry about that.

00:15:23.450 --> 00:15:26.200
All the bodies have vanished, 
leaving no proof,

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:29.570
and there is not a single survivor.

00:15:29.940 --> 00:15:33.250
Which means we can alter 
the story as we please.

00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:36.760
All we need to do is 
convince those who hear it.

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:41.140
Rimuru, a king must have no regrets.

00:15:41.140 --> 00:15:44.210
Yeah. I only did what I needed to do.

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:46.710
I came to terms with my decision long ago.

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:48.960
Very good, then.

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:53.030
All right, I will explain. Listen well.

00:15:53.030 --> 00:15:54.710
This is our story.

00:15:55.880 --> 00:15:57.560
<i>After that,</i>

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:00.300
<i>we had a very detailed discussion,</i>

00:16:00.300 --> 00:16:02.860
<i>then headed back to resume the meeting.</i>

00:16:08.180 --> 00:16:09.670
You okay?

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:15.070
You need to tell me important 
things like that beforehand!

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:17.350
Oh, I didn't tell you?

00:16:17.350 --> 00:16:19.410
Well, it's in the past now.

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:20.870
Don't just brush it off!

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:22.950
Hey, sounds like you're feeling better!

00:16:22.950 --> 00:16:26.130
Honestly... How am I going to report this?

00:16:28.190 --> 00:16:30.730
All right, we will now resume the meeting!

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:32.840
We'll start with an explanation 
of how we got here.

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:37.380
<i>Once again, I explained my 
reincarnation as a slime,</i>

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:41.030
<i>and everything that happened 
from meeting Veldora up to now.</i>

00:16:41.030 --> 00:16:42.090
<i>And then...</i>

00:16:43.280 --> 00:16:45.910
You see, your city stands in my way.

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:47.860
So I'm going to destroy it.

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:50.500
I have no interest in 
the words of a monster.

00:16:55.890 --> 00:16:57.530
Put an end to all!

00:16:58.070 --> 00:16:59.330
Disintegration!

00:17:20.650 --> 00:17:24.310
I can't believe it... 
You fought Hinata Sakaguchi?

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:27.560
Yeah. She was incredibly strong.

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:30.760
She wouldn't listen to me at all.

00:17:30.760 --> 00:17:34.070
She was like a cruel, cold-blooded killer.

00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:35.450
Hmm...

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:36.450
What is it?

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:41.570
Oh, that just differs a bit from 
the information we acquired.

00:17:41.570 --> 00:17:42.580
How so?

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:48.100
She always lends a hand to 
those who depend on her.

00:17:48.660 --> 00:17:51.590
She won't waste her time on 
anyone who ignores her advice,

00:17:51.910 --> 00:17:56.590
but her way of thinking is 
quite reasonable and rational.

00:17:58.940 --> 00:18:03.790
Hmm... Leave it to Blumund's Guildmaster, 
a man who excels at intel-gathering.

00:18:03.790 --> 00:18:07.240
I will testify that what you 
say matches what I have heard.

00:18:07.240 --> 00:18:09.850
It matches the information we have, as well.

00:18:10.260 --> 00:18:13.280
She is a model knight who 
has never once violated

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:15.520
the teachings of Lord Luminus.

00:18:15.520 --> 00:18:18.660
In other words, she is a true 
protector of law and order.

00:18:19.770 --> 00:18:24.160
If she's that great, why doesn't she 
try to stop the summoning ritual?

00:18:24.690 --> 00:18:27.780
Bringing children here from 
another world against their will

00:18:27.780 --> 00:18:30.740
is something that should never be tolerated.

00:18:31.850 --> 00:18:35.260
We don't know for certain whether 
or not she truly overlooked

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:38.110
summonings performed in 
other countries, do we?

00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:44.100
The magic used to summon Otherworlders

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:46.600
is a forbidden ritual that cannot 
be exposed to the public eye.

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:50.600
It is designated as a prohibited 
act by the Council of the West.

00:18:51.580 --> 00:18:56.230
Even if we asked about it, no nation 
would readily acknowledge it.

00:18:57.010 --> 00:19:00.040
So if they say it's not being 
done, that's the end of it.

00:19:00.040 --> 00:19:00.860
Correct.

00:19:01.130 --> 00:19:04.120
It's likely that the reason 
it was never mentioned to you

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:09.870
is because the teachings of Lord Luminus 
forbid making deals with monsters.

00:19:11.370 --> 00:19:13.880
So I have no chance of 
negotiating with them, huh?

00:19:14.680 --> 00:19:18.880
If the Western Holy Church 
designates us as enemies of God,

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:21.340
Hinata will go along with that, right?

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:23.000
I suppose so.

00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:30.170
Then allow me to go and take care of her.

00:19:30.170 --> 00:19:33.090
Whoa, whoa. Hinata's a tough opponent.

00:19:33.090 --> 00:19:34.860
You think you could take her?

00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:36.150
That's right, Diablo.

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:39.570
If a weakling like you is thinking of going,

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:41.600
I shall go instead and finish the job.

00:19:41.600 --> 00:19:43.910
Great Rimuru, you can leave this to me.

00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:46.330
Now, now, Miss Shion.

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:51.160
I hesitate to say this after you 
taught me how to be a secretary,

00:19:51.670 --> 00:19:55.420
but unfortunately, you cannot 
defeat this Hinata person.

00:19:55.420 --> 00:19:57.220
What a funny thing to say.

00:19:57.220 --> 00:20:00.840
Are you implying that you 
are stronger than me?

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:02.840
Then let us find out once 
and for all who is—

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:03.970
No, you will not!

00:20:05.620 --> 00:20:08.560
Veldora, were you...

00:20:08.690 --> 00:20:12.560
N-N-N-N-No, I wasn't trying 
to j-j-j-join in or anything!

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:16.480
If she's going to come here, 
there's no need for us to go there.

00:20:16.480 --> 00:20:18.070
Aw...

00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:19.880
No whining!

00:20:19.880 --> 00:20:23.080
I don't want to get on the 
Western Holy Church's bad side.

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:24.440
That goes for you guys, too.

00:20:24.440 --> 00:20:25.760
I am sorry.

00:20:28.140 --> 00:20:33.080
Now, that concludes the debate on 
Hinata and the Western Holy Church.

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:36.460
<b>Sirius</b>

00:20:33.510 --> 00:20:36.460
Depending on what they do, 
we may end up fighting them...

00:20:36.590 --> 00:20:39.710
But for now, we'll treat them with 
caution and keep an eye on things!

00:20:40.030 --> 00:20:41.340
Right!

00:20:40.030 --> 00:20:41.340
Very well.

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:46.460
Playing dumb won't help you. 
I received an anonymous tip.

00:20:47.110 --> 00:20:48.050
Anonymous?

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:51.600
There are eyes all over 
the Kingdom of Engrassia.

00:20:52.650 --> 00:20:55.080
<i>Someone sold me out to Hinata.</i>

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:58.520
<i>There aren't many people who 
know I killed Shizu-san.</i>

00:20:59.160 --> 00:21:00.360
<i>The only suspects are...</i>

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:02.220
<i>Notice.</i>

00:21:02.220 --> 00:21:04.940
<i>The most likely suspect is...</i>

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:10.010
<i>That's right, Raphael-san. 
The same guy I was thinking of.</i>

00:21:10.010 --> 00:21:11.370
<i>So it seems.</i>

00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:14.620
<i>But if it is him, what's he after?</i>

00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:17.800
<i>To get Hinata and me to fight 
and get rid of one of us?</i>

00:21:17.800 --> 00:21:20.040
<i>To stop me from getting back to my town?</i>

00:21:20.040 --> 00:21:21.380
<i>To lure out Hinata?</i>

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:23.880
<i>Or perhaps... all of the above.</i>

00:21:24.140 --> 00:21:26.840
<i>Seriously? That's getting too greedy.</i>

00:21:27.490 --> 00:21:28.480
Rimuru?

00:21:29.020 --> 00:21:30.260
Oh, sorry.

00:21:30.740 --> 00:21:32.440
I was thinking about something.

00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:35.050
Now, let's get down to business.

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:40.860
<i>The time had finally come 
to bring up the agenda</i>

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:43.070
<i>that would determine the fate of Tempest.</i>

00:21:47.890 --> 00:21:49.290
Ramiris?!

00:21:51.340 --> 00:21:53.060
What the heck's going on?

00:21:53.830 --> 00:21:55.790
I heard everything!

00:21:56.180 --> 00:21:57.790
This country, Tempest...

00:21:58.140 --> 00:21:59.620
is doomed to fall!

00:21:59.620 --> 00:22:00.590
Wha...

00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:04.580
What did you say?!

00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:41.020
<b>Ramiris's <u>Warning</u></b>

00:23:37.090 --> 00:23:39.960
<i>Next time, "Ramiris's Warning."</i>
